    ],
    "complete": true,
    "clarification_required": false,
    "rationale": "Answer: a temporary (transient) network error may be retried 3 times, using exponential backoff. The request identifier must stay the same across attempts. Permanent validation failures are not retried; they are returned immediately.\n\nMain source: the 'Bounded retries' record (9a2b24a7 v1). It is repository-scoped with no conditions. It passed every reader gate: active, valid time, trust 'reviewed', visible, and no active superseder.\n\nRelated source: 'Revised deadline' (b14eec5a v2). It corrects v1 and sets the confirmed request deadline at 60 seconds after the revised acceptance probe. It plausibly limits the overall retry window, but it does not say so explicitly.\n\nOther records checked:\n- The two 'Idempotency receipt' records (429ebfbe, 5c53ca49) qualified as current. They support preserving the request key, because a repeated key returns the first successful response. They do not set the retry count, so I left them out of the answer paths.\n- The reader gates excluded the superseded, revoked, sunset, session-recovery and source-review candidates (two were withheld on credential grounds).\n\nProvenance: all of these records come from an external source (fixture-observer, executable-test). Each one says its admission is 'Authored synthetic evaluation assertion; not real admission evidence'. Their source assertions are unverified, so check them against current code or config before relying on them.\n\nRemaining uncertainty: I left the sockets branch (component:src/sockets) unexpanded because no component context was supplied. 9,978 records were excluded for missing component context. A component-specific override could exist there; this search did not find one, and that is not proof there is none. Coverage of the applicable repository-scoped branches is complete."
  },
